&lt;p&gt;In current practice, usage of the term case most likely refers to the use of uppercase (capital) or lowercase letters. See some examples below. In &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20150218042642/http:/typophile.com/wiki/Letterpress"&gt;letterpress&lt;/a&gt; practice, case refers to the physical box (case), usually wooden, that a given set of letters is stored. Capital letters were stored in the upper (top) case and lowercase letters were stored in the lower (bottom) case.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Examples:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ALL CAPS &amp;ndash; All letters are capitalized.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>